/*! \page inputs Input Parameters
@brief Description of the sedExnerFoam input parameters

\tableofcontents

The input parameters for sedExnerFoam are numerous and are modifiable through different files in the current working directory. Some of the files are identical to other OpenFOAM solvers and won't be described in details herein. This is the case for the files:

\verbatim
system/blockMeshDict
system/controlDict
system/fvSchemes
system/fvSolution
constant/g
constant/dynamicMeshDict
\endverbatim

The file 'blockMeshDict' contains the description of the base mesh (see \ref meshgen, and createGeometry.py for cases that post-process the blockMesh points to set the initial bed shape). The file 'controlDict' contains the runtime parameters such as the timestep and the output interval. The file 'fvSchemes' describes the numerical schemes for the different differential operators (temporal, divergence, laplacian). The file 'fvSolution' describes the algebraic solvers, the associated tolerances, and the PIMPLE algorithm controls, including the sedExnerFoam-specific sub-iteration keywords described in \ref pimpleExnerParams below. The file 'g' contains the gravity vector. The file 'dynamicMeshDict' configures the ALE mesh motion solver used to deform the mesh so that the bed boundary follows the Exner equation (see \ref ALE_approach in \ref governingEq); the patches listed under 'sedimentBedPatches' (see \ref bedConfig below) must be declared as moving boundaries there.

The files that contain the specific input parameters for sedExnerFoam are:

\verbatim
constant/transportProperties
constant/suspensionProperties
constant/bedloadProperties
\endverbatim

\section transportProps File transportProperties

parameter   | description                            | required | default | units  |
------------|------------------------------------------|----------|---------|--------|
nu          | fluid kinematic viscosity                 | yes      | -       | m^2/s  |
rhoF        | fluid density                             | no       | 1000    | kg/m^3 |
rhoS        | sediment density                          | yes      | -       | kg/m^3 |
dS          | sediment grain diameter                   | yes      | -       | m      |
CsMax       | maximum sediment volume fraction (1-porosity) | yes  | -       | -      |
Sc          | turbulent Schmidt number for suspended sediment | no | 1      | -      |
reposeAngle | granular material angle of repose, used for avalanche bedload and (if not overridden) for the critical Shields slope correction | no | 32 | deg (must be in ]0,90[) |

CsMax is also used, together with morphoAccFactor, in the Exner equation (see exnerEqn.H and \ref bedload in \ref governingEq).

\section suspensionProps File suspensionProperties

parameter         | description                                         | required | default    | units |
------------------|------------------------------------------------------|----------|------------|-------|
suspension        | switch on/off suspended load transport                | yes      | -          | on/off |
MULESformulation  | use MULES for the Cs advection instead of the classical implicit scheme | no | off | on/off |
diffusivity       | turbulent or effective (nu+turbulent) diffusivity for Cs | no    | turbulent  | turbulent/effective |
CsbMax            | max. reference sediment volume fraction (erosion condition, Van Rijn) | no | min(CsMax,0.3) | - |

Optional sub-dictionary 'wallDiffusivity' (near-bed saltation diffusivity correction):

parameter | description                  | default |
----------|------------------------------|---------|
alpha     | near-bed diffusivity amplitude | 0     |
beta      | decay coefficient              | 5     |
gamma     | Nikuradse roughness coefficient (ks = gamma*dS) | 2.5 |

If the sub-dictionary 'wallDiffusivity' is absent, this correction is disabled.

\section bedloadProps File bedloadProperties

This dictionary configures the sediment bed itself (instantiating a sedimentBed object, see sedimentBed.C) as well as the bedload transport and Exner equation models.

\subsection bedConfig Bed existence and motion

parameter          | description                                                       | required | default |
-------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------|----------|---------|
sedimentBed        | switch on/off the sediment bed entirely (finite area mesh, bedload, Exner equation) | yes | - (on/off) |
sedimentBedPatches | list of mesh patch names forming the sediment bed (used to build the finite area mesh); must be consistent with the moving patches declared in dynamicMeshDict | yes, if sedimentBed=on | - |
bedMotion          | on: the bed moves (Exner equation deforms the mesh); off: bedload/Shields are still computed but the bed does not move | no | on |
rigidBed           | on: a non-erodible layer limits erosion/bedload where the sediment layer thickness vanishes (see HsedBed field, rigidBed treatment in bedload.H, CsEqn.H, balanceBedload.H) | no | off |

If sedimentBed=on, the gravity vector must point into the bed (consistency check performed at startup: g & faceAreaNormals > 0 on every bed face, otherwise a FatalError is raised).

\subsection saturationParams Bedload saturation (sub-dictionary 'saturation')

parameter | description                              | required (if saturation present) | default |
----------|--------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------|---------|
type      | saturation model                            | no                                 | explicit |
Tsat      | saturation time                             | yes, unless type=none              | - (s)   |
Lsat      | saturation length                           | yes, unless type=none              | - (m)   |

Valid values for 'type': implicit1D, explicit, semiImplicit, none (see bedload.H). If the 'saturation' sub-dictionary is absent entirely, no saturation length/time is used (qb = qsat directly, equivalent to type=none).

\subsection exnerAdvectionParams Bedload flux scheme (sub-dictionary 'exnerAdvection')

parameter | description                                                   | default  |
----------|------------------------------------------------------------------|----------|
qbScheme  | interpolation scheme for the shear-stress bedload flux on faMesh edges (centered or upwind) | upwind |
qavScheme | interpolation scheme for the avalanche bedload flux on faMesh edges (centered or upwind)    | centered |

If the 'exnerAdvection' sub-dictionary is absent, the defaults above apply.

\subsection bedloadModelParams Sub-dictionary 'bedloadModel'

parameter | description                                                        | default     |
----------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------|-------------|
type      | bedload transport model (see bedloadModels)                           | MeyerPeter  |
onEdge    | compute the avalanche bedload flux directly on faMesh edges instead of on faces | off |

If the 'bedloadModel' sub-dictionary is absent, type=MeyerPeter is used with onEdge=off.

\subsection critShieldsParams Sub-dictionary 'criticalShieldsModel'

parameter | description                                                        | default      |
----------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------|
type      | critical Shields number model (see criticalShieldsModels); the special value 'readFromFile' reads a user-provided non-uniform critShields field from \<time\>/finite-area/critShields instead of computing it, and disables the slope correction in bedload.H | fixedValue |
value     | constant critical Shields number (only used when type=fixedValue)     | 0.047        |

If the 'criticalShieldsModel' sub-dictionary is absent, type=fixedValue with value=0.047 is used.

\subsection filterExnerParams Sub-dictionary 'filterExner'

parameter | description                                                        | default      |
----------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------|
type      | filter formulation applied to the bed level increment dH (none, dZDiffusive, JohnsonZyserman) | dZDiffusive |
alpha     | filter diffusivity coefficient                                        | 0.1          |
Nfilt     | number of filter passes                                               | 3            |

If the 'filterExner' sub-dictionary is absent, or type=none, no filtering of dH is applied.

\subsection filterShieldsParams Sub-dictionary 'filterShields'

parameter | description                                                        | default      |
----------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------|
switch    | on/off spatial filtering of the Shields number                        | off          |
alpha     | filter diffusivity coefficient                                        | 0.1          |
Nfilt     | number of filter passes                                               | 3            |

If the 'filterShields' sub-dictionary is absent, filtering is off.

\subsection otherBedloadParams Other bedloadProperties keywords

parameter        | description                                                    | required | default |
-----------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------|----------|---------|
morphoAccFactor  | morphological acceleration factor applied to dVsed in the Exner equation | no | 1 |
maxCoBed         | max. fraction of the local first fluid cell height that the bed displacement dH may reach in one time step; bounds the time step via bedCourantNo.H (see \ref bed_courant in \ref governingEq) | no | 0.3 |
fixedFaPatches   | list of finite-area patch names where the bed displacement is forced to zero (vertices shared with these patches do not move, see meshMove.H) | no | empty list |
ABorder          | Adams-Bashforth order used to integrate the Exner equation: 0 (Euler explicit) or 1 | no | 0 |

\section pimpleExnerParams PIMPLE sub-dictionary: sub-iteration controls

These keywords are read directly from the PIMPLE sub-dictionary of system/fvSolution (not from bedloadProperties):

parameter               | description                                                    | default |
------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------|---------|
nOuterCorrectors        | standard PIMPLE keyword; nOuterCorrectors > 1 activates the PIMPLE-Exner sub-iteration (see \ref pimple_exner in \ref governingEq) | 1 |
moveMeshOuterCorrectors | standard PIMPLE keyword; must be 'yes' for the bed to actually move at every sub-iteration, otherwise only the first outer iteration updates the mesh and a warning is printed at the start of the run | - |
zbRelax                 | under-relaxation factor applied to the bed level increment dH across sub-iterations, in ]0, 1] | 1.0 |
zbTol                   | convergence tolerance (in m) on max\|dH - dH_prev\| between sub-iterations, used only for reporting (not to stop the loop early) | 1e-6 |

With nOuterCorrectors = 1, the behaviour is unchanged from a version without the sub-iteration feature.

*/
